	// THE PASS IS THE WHOLE PROOF. Nobody is asked who is calling, and an `Authorization` header
	// sent anyway is not read. A folder outside the linked folder answers `link_not_found`, as an id
	// nobody minted does: the pass opens that one folder and what is below it, and nothing beside it.
	//
	// WHAT IS LISTED is what the folder holds now, folders first, then by name as a person reads it,
	// then by id. Nothing hidden or in Trash is listed, and a folder in Trash, or below one, answers
	// `link_not_found`.
	//
	// A PASS ENDS. One hour after it was given it answers `link_pass_ended`, and the viewer opens the
	// link again. When the link expires or its owner ends it, the pass ends with it, and the answer
	// says which. A one-time link spent at its opening does not end its pass.
	//
	// EACH PAGE IS A LOOK, AND IT IS RECORDED (decision 0675): one line by the platform named
	// `storage`, for nobody, about nobody, its target the folder listed.
	//
	// IT IS LIMITED BY HOW OFTEN IT IS CALLED, NEVER BY WHO CALLS (decision 0732), as `openLink` is.
