// file keeps its id, its name and its place; every earlier version stays in its history. The
// same act as `startVersionUpload`, asked of a file in the company's tree.
//
// THE BYTES NEVER COME THROUGH THIS API: starting answers how they go up, in parts of
// `part_bytes` each, every part sent to an address asked for one at a time. Until the upload
// is completed the file is as it was.
//
// THE LIMIT IS THE COMPANY'S, read when the upload starts: a version over it is stopped with
// `file_too_large`, and `over_limit` carries both numbers. `allow_over_limit_once` changes
// nothing here, and passing the limit once with an allowed request is declared for a new file
// only.
//
// THE SPACE IS THE COMPANY'S: the new version counts against the company's storage, never a
// member's own, and `quota_full` names it: `full_storage` is `company_storage`.
//
