// app structures — inside System Storage, or an app's object wherever it sits — is that app's
// to save (`managed_by_app`). A file in Trash and a file of a person's own are not found here.
//
// A LOCK DOES NOT STOP IT: a lock is a strong warning at the moment of saving, never a
// refusal. `lock` in this answer IS the warning: somebody else's lock in force on the file,
// the "Locked by Tom · since 14:20" to show before the parts go up. The upload has started
// either way: going on saves the version over the lock, and stopping leaves the file as it
// was. `lock` is `null` when nobody holds one, an expired lock included, and when the lock
// is your own, since a lock warns everyone else.
//
// SHOWING A LOCK IS ONE LOOK at the file, about nobody. A start that shows none writes no
// line, since a write that has only begun writes none.
//
// AN UPLOAD NOBODY FINISHES IS SWEPT after a week, parts and all, and the file stays as it
// was.
//
