// THE SECRET IS THE WHOLE PROOF, and a password when its owner set one. A link names nobody,
// and nobody is asked who is calling: an `Authorization` header sent anyway is not read. It
// opens exactly the one item the link was made for, read-only, and nothing beside it.
//
// ONE LINK, WHOEVER MADE IT: a person's (`createLink`) opens their file as it is now; an app's,
// minted for a visitor, opens the one version it was minted for.
//
// A PASSWORD IS ASKED BEFORE ANYTHING IS SHOWN. Without one, `link_password_required`; a wrong
// one, `link_password_wrong` — "That password isn't right — try again." — and nothing else.
//
// A LINK THAT OPENS NOTHING SAYS WHY, because whoever holds its secret was handed it:
// `link_expired`, `link_already_used` (a one-time link) or `link_ended_by_its_owner`. A secret
// no link has answers `link_not_found`, and so does a link whose item is gone, hidden or in Trash.
//
// EACH OPENING IS COUNTED, and the first one spends a one-time link. An answer refused for any
// reason above counts nothing and spends nothing. A sealed file opens as a stated refusal, with no
// address: `read.sealed` is true, and it is counted. A one-time link to a folder is spent at its
// first opening too: opened again it answers `link_already_used`, while the first viewer's pass
// still browses until it ends.
//
// IT IS LIMITED BY HOW OFTEN IT IS CALLED, NEVER BY WHO CALLS (decision 0732). The server counts
// calls a minute from one address and from everyone together, and answers 429 past either, with
// the seconds to wait.
//
// Takes a body of the `application/json` content type.
//
// Corresponds with POST /link-openings (the `OpenLink` operationId).
func (c *Client) OpenLink(ctx context.Context, body OpenLinkJSONRequestBody, reqEditors ...RequestEditorFn) (*http.Response, error) {
	req, err := NewOpenLinkRequest(c.Server, body)
	if err != nil {
		return nil, err
	}
	req = req.WithContext(ctx)
	if err := c.applyEditors(ctx, req, reqEditors); err != nil {
		return nil, err
	}
	return c.Client.Do(req)
}

// GetPersonalStorage Your personal storage, and the id of its tree
//
// THE TREE HAS AN ID OF ITS OWN, AND THIS IS WHERE IT IS READ. Everything at the top of your
// personal storage sits in the tree itself, and a call that puts something there — a new
// folder, an upload, a move — names the tree by this id, exactly as it would name a folder.
//
// NOTHING IS EVER MEANT BY LEAVING A PLACE OUT. A request that says where something goes
// always says it with an id, so a forgotten field can never quietly mean "the top".
//
// THE TREE IS NOT A FOLDER. It has no name and cannot be renamed, moved, deleted, starred or
// shared; asked for as an item, it answers `not_found`. It is only ever named as the place
// something sits.
//
// Not gated: finding your own tree's id is not a look (decision 0675), so the catalogue asks
// nothing here. The door still asks for your credential, whether it was revoked, and the
// session's scope (decision 0693 rule 1). Seeing what is in the tree asks its read where it is
// first shown, in `listItems`. THIS HOLDS ONLY WHILE THREE THINGS DO, and each is pinned by a
// test. The answer carries the tree's id and nothing about what is in it: no name, no count,
// no size, no used space. It answers only the caller's own tree, and takes no id and no
// environment from the caller. And the door still refuses a missing or revoked credential and
// a scope that does not reach the call, an agent's key included (ONPLO-1964). A field about
// what is inside would make this a look that asks its read, which needs a new ruling.
//
// YOUR STORAGE IS THERE THE FIRST TIME YOU ASK. Nothing has to be set up before this call, and
// asking again answers the same id.
//
// WHILE IT IS BEING DELETED THIS SAYS SO, with `personal_storage_being_deleted`. Nothing can
// be read from it or put into it, and no second storage is made beside it.
//
// FOR AN AGENT OR A MACHINE THIS IS NOT BUILT YET. An agent works in the storage of the person
// it works for and has none of its own; which person that is does not reach Storage yet, so
// a caller that is not a person is answered `501 not_implemented`.
//
// Corresponds with GET /personal-storage (the `GetPersonalStorage` operationId).
func (c *Client) GetPersonalStorage(ctx context.Context, reqEditors ...RequestEditorFn) (*http.Response, error) {
	req, err := NewGetPersonalStorageRequest(c.Server)
	if err != nil {
		return nil, err
	}
	req = req.WithContext(ctx)
	if err := c.applyEditors(ctx, req, reqEditors); err != nil {
		return nil, err
	}
	return c.Client.Do(req)
}

