// RestoreVersion Bring an old version back
//
// THE OLD VERSION COMES BACK AS THE NEWEST SAVE; NOTHING IS EVER ERASED. Restoring adds a
// version on top and never rewrites history, so what was newest a moment ago is still there,
// one entry down, and can be restored in turn.
//
// APP CONTENT IN SYSTEM STORAGE RESTORES THE SAME WAY. Storage never edits it, and
// restoring is not editing.
//
// ITS OWN PERMISSION, asked about the item: restoring an earlier version is one act, and
// holding it on a folder reaches every file inside.
//
// RESTORING THE CURRENT VERSION CHANGES NOTHING, and answers the file as it is. A version
// this file does not have is `not_found`, as an item you cannot read is; a folder has no
// history of its own (`not_a_file`).
