// CompleteUpload Finish an upload
//
// THE FILE EXISTS FROM THIS MOMENT. It appears in its folder, its first version is recorded,
// and its bytes count toward the quota — not before.
//
// NOTHING IS HALF-WRITTEN. An upload with a part missing is refused (`upload_incomplete`) and
// stays resumable; a failed completion never leaves half a file behind.
//
// THE BYTES MUST ADD UP TO WHAT WAS SAID. An upload whose parts come to another size than
// the one it started with is refused (`size_differs`): the cap and the space were judged on
// the size declared, so a file of another size is one nobody agreed to.
//
// ASKING TWICE IS SAFE. Completing an upload that is already complete answers the same file
// and changes nothing.
//
// WHERE IT LANDS IS JUDGED AGAIN HERE. A name taken while the file was going up is
// `name_taken`, and a folder deleted or moved out of your reach meanwhile is
// `parent_not_found`. Neither writes a file; start again where it may land. A taken name
// is named in the problem's `name_taken_by`, as at the start.
