	// session's scope (decision 0693 rule 1). What a member sees there is asked folder by folder,
	// where it is listed. THIS HOLDS ONLY WHILE THREE THINGS DO, and each is pinned by a test. The
	// answer carries the tree's id and nothing about what is in it: no name, no count, no size,
	// no used space. It answers only the company tree of the account environment the session is
	// in, and takes no id and no environment from the caller. And the door still refuses a
	// missing or revoked credential and a scope that does not reach the call. A field about what
	// is inside would make this a look that asks its read, which needs a new ruling.
