	// recorded as an event with its reason, which the person who held the lock can read.
	//
	// YOUR OWN LOCK IS UNLOCKED, NEVER BROKEN: it is refused here (`own_lock`), and unlocking it
	// is the file's change.
	//
	// BREAKING WHAT IS NOT LOCKED changes nothing, records nothing and answers the same.
	//
	// ITS OWN PERMISSION, `storage:file-lock.delete`, asked about the file: an Administrator's
	// act, granted on a folder or on the whole company.
	//
	// Takes a body of the `application/json` content type, and returns a wrapper object for the known response body format(s).
	//
	// Corresponds with POST /company-storage/items/{item_id}/lock/break (the `BreakCompanyFileLock` operationId).
