// GetCompanyUsageWithResponse The company storage meter
//
// ONE BAR, FROM ZERO TO THE COMPANY'S TOTAL (decision 0698). The total is 10 GB free for the
// company as a whole, which it cannot hand out, plus every block it bought. Bought space
// lands here, and only bought space is ever given to a member.
//
// SEGMENTED THE SAME WAY AS YOUR OWN METER: one segment per app for what it holds in the
// company area, one for the company's folders, one for what members drew into their
// Personal storage beyond their own free 5 GB — counted here once, never twice — and Onplo's
// own overhead as its own labelled line. What the company's own holds that is not a file is
// counted since 17 November 2026, from what each service reports (ONPLO-5690), as `getUsage`
// says; until then this meter was files alone. The drawn line counts what is reported for
// each member with their files, and splits each member's excess as that member's own bytes
// split, a reported number as current.
//
// OVER THE TOTAL NOTHING IS DELETED, as with your own. New things in the company area of
// every app are refused with `quota_full` naming `company_storage`, and so is a member's write
// that would draw from it; a member with room left in their own 5 GB can still add there.
//
// ONLY A BUSINESS ENVIRONMENT HAS ONE, and a personal environment answers
// `no_company_storage`, as `getCompanyStorage` does.
//
// Not gated: the business Storage page shows this meter at the bottom of Company
// storage to everybody in it, and the catalogue gates nothing about seeing it. Which folders
// a member may open is asked folder by folder; the meter names no folder.
//
// Returns a wrapper object for the known response body format(s).
//
// Corresponds with GET /company-storage/usage (the `GetCompanyUsage` operationId).
