// OpenLinkWithBodyWithResponse Open a link, with no account
//
// WHAT SOMEONE WITH THE LINK SEES, with no account and no sign-up: the item's name, when the
// link ends, and for a file an address its bytes are read from for a few minutes. It is the
// call behind Storage's link viewer, the page a link opens.
//
// A LINK TO A FOLDER HANDS OVER A BROWSING PASS (ruled by the spec lane on 29 October 2026,
// ONPLO-3723). The viewer then lists the folder and what is below it with `listLinkedFolder`,
// and reads a file there with `readLinkedFile`, each with the pass and never the secret again.
// So the secret and the password are each asked once. The pass is held in the page's memory
// only, never in the address or a cookie. It ends one hour after it is given, or when the link
// ends, whichever comes first, and it opens nothing outside the linked folder.
//
// THE ADDRESS A LINK OPENS AT is Storage's link viewer, under `onplo.com/app/storage/`
// (decision 0542), with the link's secret after `#`: `https://onplo.com/app/storage/link#<secret>`.
// A browser never sends what follows `#`, so the secret reaches no server's log, no proxy and
// no `Referer`. The viewer reads it there and sends it here, in the body, which is why this is
// a `POST`. Which site address the server writes is its configuration, never its code.
//
// THE SECRET IS THE WHOLE PROOF, and a password when its owner set one. A link names nobody,
// and nobody is asked who is calling: an `Authorization` header sent anyway is not read. It
// opens exactly the one item the link was made for, read-only, and nothing beside it.
//
// ONE LINK, WHOEVER MADE IT: a person's (`createLink`) opens their file as it is now; an app's,
// minted for a visitor, opens the one version it was minted for.
//
// A PASSWORD IS ASKED BEFORE ANYTHING IS SHOWN. Without one, `link_password_required`; a wrong
// one, `link_password_wrong` — "That password isn't right — try again." — and nothing else.
//
// A LINK THAT OPENS NOTHING SAYS WHY, because whoever holds its secret was handed it:
// `link_expired`, `link_already_used` (a one-time link) or `link_ended_by_its_owner`. A secret
// no link has answers `link_not_found`, and so does a link whose item is gone, hidden or in Trash.
//
// EACH OPENING IS COUNTED, and the first one spends a one-time link. An answer refused for any
// reason above counts nothing and spends nothing. A sealed file opens as a stated refusal, with no
// address: `read.sealed` is true, and it is counted. A one-time link to a folder is spent at its
// first opening too: opened again it answers `link_already_used`, while the first viewer's pass
// still browses until it ends.
//
// IT IS LIMITED BY HOW OFTEN IT IS CALLED, NEVER BY WHO CALLS (decision 0732). The server counts
// calls a minute from one address and from everyone together, and answers 429 past either, with
// the seconds to wait.
//
// Takes any type of body and a specified content type, and returns a wrapper object for the known response body format(s).
//
// Corresponds with POST /link-openings (the `OpenLink` operationId).
func (c *ClientWithResponses) OpenLinkWithBodyWithResponse(ctx context.Context, contentType string, body io.Reader, reqEditors ...RequestEditorFn) (*OpenLinkResponse, error) {
	rsp, err := c.OpenLinkWithBody(ctx, contentType, body, reqEditors...)
	if err != nil {
		return nil, err
	}
	return ParseOpenLinkResponse(rsp)
}

