// GetPersonalStorageWithResponse Your personal storage, and the id of its tree
//
// THE TREE HAS AN ID OF ITS OWN, AND THIS IS WHERE IT IS READ. Everything at the top of your
// personal storage sits in the tree itself, and a call that puts something there — a new
// folder, an upload, a move — names the tree by this id, exactly as it would name a folder.
//
// NOTHING IS EVER MEANT BY LEAVING A PLACE OUT. A request that says where something goes
// always says it with an id, so a forgotten field can never quietly mean "the top".
//
// THE TREE IS NOT A FOLDER. It has no name and cannot be renamed, moved, deleted, starred or
// shared; asked for as an item, it answers `not_found`. It is only ever named as the place
// something sits.
//
// Not gated: finding your own tree's id is not a look (decision 0675), so the catalogue asks
// nothing here. The door still asks for your credential, whether it was revoked, and the
// session's scope (decision 0693 rule 1). Seeing what is in the tree asks its read where it is
// first shown, in `listItems`. THIS HOLDS ONLY WHILE THREE THINGS DO, and each is pinned by a
// test. The answer carries the tree's id and nothing about what is in it: no name, no count,
// no size, no used space. It answers only the caller's own tree, and takes no id and no
// environment from the caller. And the door still refuses a missing or revoked credential and
// a scope that does not reach the call, an agent's key included (ONPLO-1964). A field about
// what is inside would make this a look that asks its read, which needs a new ruling.
//
// YOUR STORAGE IS THERE THE FIRST TIME YOU ASK. Nothing has to be set up before this call, and
// asking again answers the same id.
//
// WHILE IT IS BEING DELETED THIS SAYS SO, with `personal_storage_being_deleted`. Nothing can
// be read from it or put into it, and no second storage is made beside it.
//
// FOR AN AGENT OR A MACHINE THIS IS NOT BUILT YET. An agent works in the storage of the person
// it works for and has none of its own; which person that is does not reach Storage yet, so
// a caller that is not a person is answered `501 not_implemented`.
//
// Returns a wrapper object for the known response body format(s).
//
// Corresponds with GET /personal-storage (the `GetPersonalStorage` operationId).
func (c *ClientWithResponses) GetPersonalStorageWithResponse(ctx context.Context, reqEditors ...RequestEditorFn) (*GetPersonalStorageResponse, error) {
	rsp, err := c.GetPersonalStorage(ctx, reqEditors...)
	if err != nil {
		return nil, err
	}
	return ParseGetPersonalStorageResponse(rsp)
}

// ListArchivedWithResponse What is archived
