// StartRewindWithBodyWithResponse Rewind a folder to a moment
//
// EVERYTHING UNDER THE FOLDER GOES BACK TO HOW IT STOOD AT THE MOMENT — or everything in your
// personal storage, when `parent_id` is the tree's id. Ask for the preview first: it says
// what this will change.
//
// NOTHING IS ERASED. Each file comes back as its newest version, so history is never
// rewritten; a file made after the moment goes to Trash. Shares and links stay attached and
// reach the restored version. Branches survive it, and the version line moves forward to older
// content (decision 0458).
//
// LEFT OUT: a folder backed by outside storage, or synced, whose sync pauses.
//
// IT RUNS IN THE BACKGROUND. The answer is the Rewind as it starts; ask for it again to see
// it finish. While it runs, the folder can be read and nothing can be written into it.
//
// A REWIND CAN ALWAYS BE REWOUND. What stood before it is kept first, so a Rewind of the same
// folder to `started_at` undoes it.
//
// ONE AT A TIME. A Rewind already running on this folder, or on one around it or inside it,
// answers 409 `rewind_running`.
//
