// CreateGrantWithBodyWithResponse Share an item
//
// GIVE A PERSON OR A TEAM A ROLE ON THIS ITEM: Viewer, Editor or Manager. Commenter is
// deliberately not offered — Storage has nowhere to leave a comment yet, and a role that
// does nothing is a promise the app cannot keep.
//
// MOST ACCESS IS TEMPORARY AND NOBODY REMEMBERS TO REMOVE IT. `access_until` is the moment
// this one grant ends: a date, a time and the time zone they were chosen in (decision 0650).
// It simply stops then.
//
// ON APP CONTENT THE ROLE IS VIEWER, which here means read, restore and download
// (`app_content_is_view_only`). One thing never has two editors: changing it happens in its
// own app, and sharing it for use there is that app's share, a separate act with its own
// revoke.
//
// NO ACCESS TO ANY APP FOLLOWS FROM A GRANT HERE, and none here follows from a share made in
// an app.
//
// A SHARE LETS IN, AND ONLY ADDS (decision 0650). A grant placed on an item gives its holder
// more than the folder above gives, never less: somebody who is Editor on the folder and is
// given Viewer on one file inside it is still an Editor of that file. Nobody is ever kept
// out by a smaller grant quietly replacing a bigger one.
//
// SHARING AGAIN CHANGES THE GRANT THAT IS THERE. A person or a team holds at most ONE grant
// placed directly on an item. Shared with again, their grant takes the new role and the new
// end and keeps its id. There is never a second row to clean up.
//
// SO THE ANSWER SAYS WHICH IT WAS, in `created`, and the status is `200` either way. It was
// `201` until this was ruled; "Created" for a call that may have made nothing would be a
// status that lies half the time, and a client that retried after a timeout could not tell a
// second grant from the same one.
//
// KEEP THE GRANT'S ID. Listing who already reaches an item is not declared yet, so the id
// answered here is what changes or ends this share later.
//
// NEVER AN AI AGENT'S TO DO. A share is a grant of access: an agent may prepare one and never
// hand it over.
//
// Takes any type of body and a specified content type, and returns a wrapper object for the known response body format(s).
//
// Corresponds with POST /personal-storage/items/{item_id}/grants (the `CreateGrant` operationId).
func (c *ClientWithResponses) CreateGrantWithBodyWithResponse(ctx context.Context, itemId ItemId, contentType string, body io.Reader, reqEditors ...RequestEditorFn) (*CreateGrantResponse, error) {
	rsp, err := c.CreateGrantWithBody(ctx, itemId, contentType, body, reqEditors...)
	if err != nil {
		return nil, err
	}
	return ParseCreateGrantResponse(rsp)
}

