// StartVersionUploadWithBodyWithResponse Start uploading a new version of a file
//
// REPLACE. An upload that met a taken name may go into the file that carries it instead,
// as its newest version: "the old file stays as an earlier version". The file keeps its id,
// its name and its place; every earlier version stays in its history.
//
// THE BYTES NEVER COME THROUGH THIS API, as for a new file: starting answers how the bytes
// go up, in parts of `part_bytes` each, every part sent to an address asked for one at a
// time. Until the upload is completed the file is as it was.
//
// THE LIMIT IS THE ONE A NEW FILE IS HELD TO, read when the upload starts: a version over
// it is stopped with `file_too_large`, and `over_limit` carries both numbers.
// `allow_over_limit_once` lets this one version past it in a personal account environment.
// In a business one the limit is the company's, and passing it once with an allowed request
// is declared for a new file only.
//
// A FILE OF YOUR OWN, OR ONE SHARED WITH YOU TO EDIT. "In a folder shared with you, an
// Editor may Replace too": an Editor of a file, or of a folder it sits in, may put a new
// version into it, and the old file stays as an earlier version in the owner's history.
// The permission is the same one, held over the file shared with you. THE NEW VERSION
// COUNTS AGAINST THE OWNER'S SPACE, where the file and its history live, never yours. A folder has no bytes of its
// own (`not_a_file`). Something an app structures — inside System Storage, or an app's
// object wherever it sits — is that app's to save (`managed_by_app`). A file in Trash, a
// company file and a file shared with you only to view are not found here.
//
// A LOCK DOES NOT STOP IT. A file's lock is in company storage only, and warns at a save
// rather than refusing it.
//
// AN UPLOAD NOBODY FINISHES IS SWEPT after a week, parts and all, and the file stays as it
// was.
//
// Takes any type of body and a specified content type, and returns a wrapper object for the known response body format(s).
//
// Corresponds with POST /personal-storage/items/{item_id}/version-uploads (the `StartVersionUpload` operationId).
func (c *ClientWithResponses) StartVersionUploadWithBodyWithResponse(ctx context.Context, itemId ItemId, contentType string, body io.Reader, reqEditors ...RequestEditorFn) (*StartVersionUploadResponse, error) {
	rsp, err := c.StartVersionUploadWithBody(ctx, itemId, contentType, body, reqEditors...)
	if err != nil {
		return nil, err
	}
	return ParseStartVersionUploadResponse(rsp)
}

