// GetStorageEventPreferencesWithResponse Which of Storage's own events notify you
//
// EVERY CATEGORY STORAGE POSTS UNDER, each with your three switches — in the app, by email, by
// push — and what the company set for it: `none`, `default` (a starting point you may change)
// or `required`.
//
// Not gated: it answers for the caller alone, in the account environment the credential acts
// in. What you chose in another account environment is answered there.
//
// ONLY A PERSON HAS EVENT CHOICES. An agent or a machine is refused with 403
// `ring_requires_person`, and the notifications service is asked nothing.
//
// ELEVEN CATEGORIES, one per event the Notification preferences page lists, each named by
// Storage and permanent, answered in this order:
//
//	`storage.quota-nearly-full`       your storage nearly full
//	`storage.quota-reached`           your storage full
//	`storage.sync-problem-unresolved` a sync problem the app could not resolve itself
//	`storage.shared-with-you`         someone sharing something with you
//	`storage.your-share-opened`       someone opening what you shared
//	`storage.conflict-copy-created`   a conflict copy being created
//	`storage.background-job-finished` a background job finishing: an export, a restore, a large move
//	`storage.trash-retention-ending`  something in Trash about to pass its retention window
//	`storage.legal-hold-ended`        a legal hold on a folder or file you own ending
//	`storage.upload-over-limit-waiting`   an upload over the limit waiting for you to answer
//	`storage.upload-over-limit-answered`  your upload over the limit answered, allowed or refused
//
// THE TWO UPLOAD-OVER-THE-LIMIT EVENTS happen in a business account environment only (decision
// 0758; ONPLO-4470). They are answered in a personal one too, as every app answers one list
// wherever it is asked: Keys answers its company's events the same way. Nothing is posted
// under either until an ask can be made (ONPLO-4529).
//
// A CATEGORY YOU NEVER CHOSE, where the company set nothing, answers where Storage starts it:
// on the notification icon (`in_app`), with `email` and `push` off. That is ten of the
// eleven. `storage.shared-with-you` starts with `email` on as well, Storage's one named
// exception (decision 0766, rule 3; ONPLO-2150): a share's "Notify with a message" is a mail the
// sharer asked for, and your switch still wins. None of Storage's events starts with push on.
// The example shows exactly that. A choice you made is answered as you made it.
//
// ACCOUNT'S GENERAL CHANNELS STILL DECIDE. A category with `email` on sends no email while
// email is off in Account's Notification preferences. The choice here is kept and counts
// again when the channel is back on.
//
// WHEN THE NOTIFICATIONS SERVICE CANNOT BE ASKED the answer is 503
// `notifications_unavailable`, never the choices from a copy and never where each category
// starts. The same request can be sent again.
//
// Returns a wrapper object for the known response body format(s).
//
// Corresponds with GET /storage-event-preferences (the `GetStorageEventPreferences` operationId).
func (c *ClientWithResponses) GetStorageEventPreferencesWithResponse(ctx context.Context, reqEditors ...RequestEditorFn) (*GetStorageEventPreferencesResponse, error) {
	rsp, err := c.GetStorageEventPreferences(ctx, reqEditors...)
	if err != nil {
		return nil, err
	}
	return ParseGetStorageEventPreferencesResponse(rsp)
}

